  <ym-title|Classical stationary vertices \V draft source
  correspondence><label|classical-stationary-vertices--draft-source-correspondence>

  Source pin <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. Output
  <verbatim|manuscript/existence/classical-stationary-vertices.tex>, initial
  SHA256 <verbatim|67f9608e4b073f1dc25d0178c0f13e8e8cf42b14c9cc11a26f26ad352b357a4c>.

  Targeted inspected sources, namespace YM.Stationary:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Shape/Vertex.lean>:
    <verbatim|Cruise>, <verbatim|Headers.cruise>, <verbatim|Cruise.stars>,
    <verbatim|cabinTicket>, <verbatim|launchBridge>. Cruise is explicitly
    quantitative through two fine differences; not ordinary smoothness.

    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Shape/VertexWeights.lean>:
    <verbatim|Laureate>, <verbatim|panel_plain>, <verbatim|panel_rough>,
    <verbatim|velvet_text>, <verbatim|napTax>, <verbatim|nap_cap>,
    <verbatim|velvet_sized>, <verbatim|voile>, <verbatim|ageGlimpse>,
    <verbatim|setWest>. Wilson degree3/q1 and degree4/q0; residual degree3/q2
    and degree4/q1; fine block count subtracts four powers. First rough leg
    gets no differences in winglet. Unnormalized derivative includes n! in
    textBare. Output prices a+inch<em|ell and b+inch>r with a,b before
    incoming width/budget. Penalty source napTax = 2^n<em|4>abs(cashBook G J
    n (muralRoom J*cabinTicket G D) penalty).

    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Block/Packing.lean>:
    <verbatim|through_charge>, <verbatim|shiny_steps>. Complex expansion
    costs 2^n. Weighted real stencil supplier retained explicitly.

    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/FrameEst/Stencils.lean>:
    <verbatim|crossing_stamp>, <verbatim|canopy_sits>, <verbatim|books_paid>,
    <verbatim|cashBook>. Inspected to identify weighted penalty input; NOT
    claiming the prior fixed-L local derivative chapter proves L-independent
    weighted stencil prices.

    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Shape/Exchange.lean>:
    <verbatim|quarks_act>, <verbatim|vigor_pays>, <verbatim|verge_fee>,
    <verbatim|pure_beat>, <verbatim|press_beat>, <verbatim|shaftPorts>,
    <verbatim|pennies>, <verbatim|exchangeYield>. Weighted duality avoids
    block-dimension loss. Cubic = raw tangent cubic/6; quartic = (raw tangent
    quartic minus three internal inverse-Hessian pairings)/24. Same actual
    inverse/branch recording retained. Widths eta/6,eta/8.

    <item><verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Level/Transition.lean>: consumer
    threshold inch<em|ell,inch>r\<less\>=1 and preselected Mstar.
  </itemize-minus>

  Canonical reuse: soft-curvature-receipts factorization/greyson and Wilson
  vacuum pictures. Shared background notes searched for
  Schur/stationary/vertex matches; no verified replacement found. The
  elementary stationary derivative identity is proved directly by Taylor
  expansion/polarization rather than invoking an external result. No novel
  alternate construction proposed.

  Open supplier obligations: quantitative Cruise, internal weighted discrete
  Fourier bound, L-independent real weighted penalty stencil derivatives, and
  Fourier symbol of the same inverse with Freezer price. Ordinary fixed-L
  chart bounds do not close them. This bounded unit is not the complete
  transition proof.

  Checks actually run: targeted rg/sed reads above; SHA256 capture. No new
  Lean build, axiom replay, or upstream source edit. Independent source/math
  review requested; all public approval fields remain null.

  Reviewed corrected snapshot <verbatim|3c4a930321bcd63d51403c90ec80585abfddc25d5c6308afcddf4f0c3003e6b9>:
  Hearing charge1 is L2; D_* enlarged to cover 5 exp4. Bounded independent
  mathematical/source pass received.

  Independent bounded draft review passed at
  40a22ff050d43d1df00657a9c7b2d02b2872420eb0ff2465bf2b54c1a45a5f2b
  (2026-11-12 05:23 UTC). Static inverse and selected linear-data units now
  supply each other\<#2019\>s explicit interfaces; full determinant-jet and
  finite-volume recording estimates remain separate obligations. No fresh
  Lean build.

